# ---------------- S1.2 linear network ----------------
S12 = S("S1.2",
  "A fixed network of linear gates on $W$ wires, run in eight rows per invocation and three stages, sends $(X_a,Y_a)\\mapsto(-Y_a,X_a)$ for the two data banks and restores every scratch wire $A_{ST}$, whatever the scratch wires initially hold.",
  "Make one forward invocation add $x_S$ to $y_S$ regardless of scratch contents, by subtracting the old scratch effect, adding the source's effect through copy, gather, scatter and side injection, and restoring scratch; then compose three such invocations (X to Y, inverse Y to X, X to Y).",
  M("The first two rows of the schedule remove the effect of the old scratch values, the next four add the source's effect to the target and the last two restore the scratch values, so the net change cannot depend on what the scratch wires held.", "explicit",
    "the following schedule remove the effect of the old scratch values;"),
  [
    I("S1.2.1", "If the initial side and central vectors are $a,c$, the net target change of a forward invocation is $(\\mathcal J\\mathcal V+\\mathcal R\\mathcal G)x$, independent of the initial values $a$ of the side wires $A_{ST}$ and $c$ of the central wires, because rows 0 and 1 subtract $\\mathcal Ja+\\mathcal Rc$, rows 2 to 5 add $\\mathcal R(c+\\mathcal Gx)+\\mathcal J(a+\\mathcal Vx)$ and rows 6 and 7 restore $c,a$.",
      "Rows 6 and 7 restore $c,a$.  The net target change is"),
    I("S1.2.2", "In the bit construction the central coefficient from $x_T$ to $y_S$ is $|S\\cap T|\\bmod 2$, the side wires cancel exactly the intersection-one cases, distinct triples meeting in zero or two points already have coefficient zero and the self coefficient is one, so the net map is $y_S\\gets y_S+x_S$.",
      "In the bit case, the central coefficient from $x_T$ to $y_S$ is"),
    I("S1.2.3", "In the complex construction the central coefficient is $(|S\\cap T|-1)/2$, cancelled by the side term for distinct triples meeting in zero or two points, with intersection one contributing zero and self coefficient one, so again $y_S\\gets y_S+x_S$.",
      "In the complex case, the central coefficient is $(|S\\cap T|-1)/2$."),
    I("S1.2.4", "Three stages (forward $X\\to Y$, inverse $Y\\to X$, forward $X\\to Y$) take $(x,y)$ to $(x,y+x)$, then $(-y,y+x)$, then $(-y,x)$, which is the signed exchange of $X_a$ and $Y_a$.",
      "$X\\gets X-Y$.  Starting from $(x,y)$, the three stages give"),
  ],
  page="linear-network",
  frm=["vectors-matrices-and-invertibility", "finite-field-f2-arithmetic", "permutations-and-cartesian-products", "linear-algebra-basics"],
  salient="The exchange is exact for arbitrary initial contents of every scratch wire: the net change depends only on the data, so scratch roles can later be filled with any existing rows of an array.",
  adds=[B("X_a", "data bank X", "The wire carrying the entry of the first bank at index $a$, one of $N$ such wires.", "direct"),
        B("Y_a", "data bank Y", "The wire carrying the entry of the second bank at index $a$, exchanged with $X_a$.", "direct"),
        B("A_{ST}", "side wire", "The scratch wire attached to the ordered pair of neighboring triples $(S,T)$ within one invocation.", "direct")])

# ---------------- S1.3 common frame ----------------
